From 7c67ad87bc9842a7ba73446fa760d1ec62d58304 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman Fries <baracoder@googlemail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:55:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add: move and resize tiled windows by dragging them
 anywhere

A tiled window could only be moved by its tab (frame_tab_drag) and
resized by its divider (tiling_divider_resize), each a narrow target,
while floating_move and floating_resize, bound to Super+drag, ignore
tiled windows.

window_drag and frame_resize_drag take a window grabbed anywhere on
it: a floating one moves or resizes as before, a tiled one is dragged
as its tab into the frame it is released over, or has the dividers
nearest the pointer moved, one per axis - the one on the side of the
frame the pointer is in, or the other side's at the layout edge.

ion._internal.tiled_frame_at_pointer() finds the frame, and
frame_tab_drag's generator is split out so a drag can start from a
stand-in tab.
